# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (see com.hakios.demo.plist).
# The battery (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.battery, with adsp=1): what the kernel's power source says and what
# powerd and IOPS have made of it (src/battery_test.c); then the places that show it, for screenshots:
# the home screen's status bar, the Today view with its widgets (Batteries among them), Settings >
# Battery (its Battery Percentage switched off and on again: the number beside the status bar's
# battery goes and comes back) and Battery Health & Charging, and the lock screen ("56% Charged"
# under the date).
#
# Status 2026-11-11: the status bar and the lock screen show the live charge
# (68 -> 61 percent through a soak; 51-62 percent on the lock screen, IOPS equal
# to the kernel), but the Settings pages were never reached: the boot-time cover
# sheet stays up and neither touch (a 250 ms bottom-edge swipe, the camera
# scene's swipe, a grab-drag) nor the injector's own unlock dismisses it -- the
# Darwin notification com.hakios.unlock answers "not locked" while the cover
# sheet is still on the framebuffer and its clock keeps ticking
# (logs/batui6-435.png, 10:51, 51 percent; logs/224403-run.log). So the lock
# manager and the cover sheet are out of step on this build; the battery UI
# evidence stands on the status bar, the lock screen and IOPS, and the Settings
# page waits for a proper fix to that state (the injector's unlock() is in
# userland/src/inject_sb.c).
/redwood/bin/battery_test 1
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 300 notify com.hakios.unlock wait 4 button home wait 5 swipe 0.5 0.5 0.98 0.5 300 wait 5
/redwood/bin/battery_test open prefs:root=BATTERY_USAGE
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 7 tap 0.843 0.179 wait 5 tap 0.843 0.179 wait 5 drag 0.5 0.85 0.5 0.45 2000 400 wait 5
/redwood/bin/battery_test open prefs:root=BATTERY_USAGE&path=BATTERY_HEALTH
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 8 button home wait 4 button lock wait 3 button lock wait 6
/redwood/bin/battery_test 8 15
